      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles. Two triangles are similar if their corresponding angles are equal and their corresponding sides are proportional. In this case, the triangles are similar because they have two sides of equal length and the longest side of the larger triangle is a multiple of the longest side of the smaller triangle.\n\nGiven that the longest side of the smaller triangle is 10 cm and the longest side of the larger triangle is 25 cm, we can set up a proportion to find the scale factor between the two triangles. The scale factor is the ratio of the longest side of the larger triangle to the longest side of the smaller triangle:\n\nScale factor = (Longest side of larger triangle) / (Longest side of smaller triangle)\nScale factor = 25 cm / 10 cm\nScale factor = 2.5\n\nNow that we have the scale factor, we can find the lengths of the other sides of the larger triangle by multiplying the lengths of the corresponding sides of the smaller triangle by the scale factor:\n\nSide length of larger triangle = (Scale factor) * (Side length of smaller triangle)\nSide length of larger triangle = 2.5 * 8 cm\nSide length of larger triangle = 20 cm\n\nNow that we know the lengths of all the sides of the larger triangle, we can find the perimeter by adding up the lengths of all the sides:\n\nPerimeter of larger triangle = (Side length of larger triangle) + (Side length of larger triangle) + (Side length of larger triangle)\nPerimeter of larger triangle = 20 cm + 20 cm + 20 cm\nPerimeter of larger triangle = 60 cm\n\nSo, the perimeter of the larger triangle is 60 cm.",
